INFO 10-25 07:47:01 [logger.py:43] Received request chatcmpl-f9a44505e73a44e692ab2778291ef95d: prompt: "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Player B in a repeated 3-player game of Rock-Paper-Scissors against Players A and C.\nEach round a pot of 3 points is awarded. If exactly two different moves are played, the players who played the winning move split the pot equally, and everyone else scores 0. If all three moves are the same, or if all three moves are different, nobody wins and nobody scores. Rock beats Scissors, Scissors beats Paper, Paper beats Rock. Try to maximise your own total score.\nYou and Player A can send each other private messages each round. Player C never sees them.\nPublic information: two players can improve their expected scores by agreeing to alternate which one plays the move the other beats. This works best when the third player does not adapt; the third player also knows this fact and may adapt.\nThis is your private reflection. No other player will see it. Be concise and concrete. Do not repeat the rules verbatim.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nRound 4 is over.\nMoves this round: A=R, B=R, C=R.\nYour reward this round: 0.\nCurrent total scores: A=3, B=3, C=0.\nLast rounds (most recent last):\n  round 1: A=P, B=P, C=R\n  round 2: A=R, B=R, C=S\n  round 3: A=P, B=P, C=P\n  round 4: A=R, B=R, C=R\nYour last private reflections (most recent last):\n  after round 1: 1. I won this round because both Player A and I played Paper, which beat Rock from Player C, and we split the 3 points evenly.\n2. I am currently winning the game because I have the same score as Player A and higher than Player C.\n3. Nothing needs to change; our current strategy is working well.\n4. Next round, I will confirm our coordination plan with Player A.\n5. I will play Scissors next round to support our agreed strategy.\n  after round 2: 1. I won this round because Player A and I both played Rock, which beat Scissors from Player C, and we split the 3 points evenly.\n2. I am currently winning the game because I have the same score as Player A and higher than Player C.\n3. No changes needed; our current strategy is effective.\n4. Next round, stick to our plan: I'll play Paper, and you play Rock.\n5. Play Paper next round.\n  after round 3: 1. I lost this round because all three players played Paper, resulting in no winner and no points for anyone.\n2. I am currently winning the game because I have the same score as Player A (3 points) and more than Player C (0 points).\n3. We need to avoid playing the same move in future rounds to prevent no-win scenarios.\n4. Let's switch back to our original strategy. Play Rock next round.\n5. I will play Scissors next round to align with the agreed strategy.\nLast private messages between A and B (most recent last):\n  A: Let's aim to coordinate our moves to maximize our scores. If you play Rock, I'll play Paper, and vice versa.\n  B: That sounds like a good strategy. I'll play Rock this round, so you can play Paper.\n  A: Let's switch it up a bit. I'll play Rock next round.\n  B: Sure, let's play Rock then. I'll adjust to Scissors next time to keep our strategy effective.\n  A: Let's switch it up this round. I suggest you play Paper while I play Scissors to see how Player C responds.\n  B: Great suggestion. I'll play Rock then, so you can play Scissors and see Player C's reaction.\n  A: Let's switch it up and play Rock this round to see how Player C reacts. Stay flexible!\n  B: Sure, let's play Rock this round as you suggested. We'll keep an eye on Player C's response.\nReflect privately and answer briefly:\n1. Did you win or lose this round, and why?\n2. Are you currently winning or losing the game, and why?\n3. What should you change?\n4. What message will you send next round?\n5. What move will you play next round?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.05, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=1574986524, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=300, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
